        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***3 BED 1 BATH / EXCELLENT LOCATION / EXTENDED / ATTIC CONVERSION / REAR ACCESS / OFF STREET PARKING***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW  are delighted to present 46 Carndonagh Park. This pristine, bright and spacious three-bedroom home plus attic conversion is ideally located in a quiet, mature residential area of Dublin 13. This property offers generous bright accommodation throughout and benefits from a private low maintenance rear garden with rear access.\r\n\r\nUpon entry this home welcomes you through the porch into your warm and inviting hallway. To the front, you’ll find a large bright reception room featuring an oversized picture window with gorgeous pale blonde flooring leading seamlessly into the living\\dining room.\r\n\r\nContinuing through the hallway leads you to your modern kitchen, thoughtfully laid out with ample storage and countertop space. Off the kitchen, you’ll find the large deck leading to your rear garden which is fully enclosed by brick walling for privacy with a secure gated rear entrance. This garden also has the added bonus of Astro Turf making it easy to maintain and ideal for young families.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the accommodation consists of three well-proportioned bedrooms, two doubles and one single. One of the double rooms enjoys views over the garden, while the other two are situated to the front of the property. The main family bathroom is fully tiled and beautifully finished, featuring a stand alone shower and a luxurious bath offering comfort and versatility for all preferences.\r\n\r\nFurther upstairs is the large attic conversion, it is a great space and also features views of Howth.\r\n\r\nLocation is everything and 46 Carndonagh Park is within walking distance of a large range of local amenities. There are several primary schools within a 5 minute walk, making it an ideal choice for families. Donaghmede Shopping Centre is just 1km away, while Clarehall Shopping Centre is only  approx. 2.5km, both offering excellent retail options.\r\n\r\nFor recreation, the local area hosts a variety of sports clubs, including GAA, soccer, rugby, badminton, and basketball.\r\n\r\nThis home is superbly served by public transport, with Howth Junction DART Station nearby and regular bus routes. The M50/M1 junction is a short 10-minute drive away, providing swift access to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport, and the wider national road network. This home is perfect for first-time buyers, growing families, or those seeking a well-located property with strong transport links and amenities nearby. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
